   GPL BOUNDARY (load-bearing — do NOT collapse this):
   Paper Platform is ARCHITECTED to interact with prar-agent ONLY through its
   stable, out-of-process HTTP/WebSocket API. Every such call is funnelled
   through the single adapter module `orchestrator/prar_bridge.py`. NO Paper
   Platform module imports prar-agent's internal Python symbols (its `core/*`,
   `llm/*`, `memory/*`, `tools/*`). This out-of-process boundary is DESIGNED to
   keep the two as separate programs communicating at arm's length and to REDUCE
   the risk that Paper Platform is treated as a GPL derivative work of the
   engine — which would leave Paper Platform free to be distributed under
   Apache-2.0. Conversely, importing engine internals would almost certainly
   make Paper Platform a derivative work and force it to GPL-3.0, so the
   boundary is enforced by `contracts/test_boundary.py`.
   NOTE: whether the two are in fact "mere aggregation" rather than a single
   combined program is a LEGAL determination that depends on the actual
   distribution structure and cannot be concluded from "communicates over HTTP"
   alone. This note is an engineering risk judgment, NOT legal advice — confirm
   with qualified counsel before redistributing.

